  "DescIdentified": {
    "type": "cexolocstring",
    "value": {
      "0": "The torc given by Lindir of the Hall of Fire to those he takes as students. The notation on it is the opening phrase of a lay nobody living has heard the end of; he sets it about the neck of a singer so that the first thing they wear is an unfinished sentence. Those who wear it find their voice carries further than it has any right to."
    }
  },
  "Description": {
    "type": "cexolocstring",
    "value": {
      "0": "A thin silver torc of Rivendell work, open at the front, chased along its whole length with a line of notation too small to read at arm's length."
    }
  },
